      "message": "fix(ui): one tool preview, a full points table, plain words on the profile page\n\nThe Profile tab of the tool editor has no second side view. The one\nto-scale preview draws the draft of the tab: a drawn holder as the bands\nthat the collision check sweeps, a drawn cutter as the steel outline.\n\nThe points table keeps a least height of 150 px. egui gave the nested\nscroll area only the space left in the view, so a table low on the page\nshowed about two rows. The grid has no 40 px least column width, so the\nremove buttons stay in a narrow pane. The tab row and the file buttons\nwrap.\n\nThe page says \"In use: ...\" in place of \"landed\", and the table headers\nand the holder line use plain words.\n\nRefs #2007\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
